55,3,1,talk,Minako,,"We have three options: A is Fixed Day Allocation, B is a Booking Calendar with distance-based costs, and C is a Primary Keeper.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A removes the ""asking for favors"" problem, but Option B is more precise for the fuel imbalance Shion mentioned.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A would solve my weekly trip collapses. I'd know exactly which days the car is mine.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Shion,,"Option B is the most logical for costs, but Daisuke already said he hates the time spent recording runs.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,I really don't like Option B. The recording sounds like a nightmare.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Minako,,Option C puts the burden on one person. That might be too much for one of us to handle.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, but it eliminates the group friction. One person is the gatekeeper, and the others just pay per trip.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"In Option C, would the Primary Keeper ensure the car is clean? Because that's my main priority.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, probably, but Option A is the cleanest break. No one asks, no one records, you just have your days.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,Option A sounds the easiest. No more evening planning sessions.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Minako,,"Option A is a fixed monthly share, which is simple, but it doesn't account for the fuel gap Shion found.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"True, but the ""social cost"" of Option B's recording is too high based on our findings.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I'm leaning toward A. Stability over precision.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Shion,,"If we can't do B, A is the next most logical. It's a fair, if blunt, instrument.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'm definitely voting for A.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Minako,,I'll vote for A as well. It's the most stable for the group's harmony.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I agree. Let's prioritize the relationship over the last few yen. I vote A.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I vote A.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Shion,,I'll go with A. It's the most efficient way to stop the arguing.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,A for me too.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
